颗粒大小以外的因素来分离组分。

13
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:58,900
These focus on properties such as solubility, polarity, and reactivity.
这些技术着眼于溶解度、极性和反应性等性质。

14
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:03,420
The technique we will go over in this tutorial is called extraction.
我们在本期教程中要讲的技术叫做萃取。

15
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:08,040
Extraction is a technique that uses a two-phase system to separate mixtures.
萃取是一种利用两相体系来分离混合物的技术。

16
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:13,620
The most common form is a liquid-liquid extraction, and in this context, the two-phase system
最常见的形式是液液萃取，在这种情况下，两相体系

17
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:17,120
will be an organic phase and an aqueous phase.
就是有机相和水相。

18
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:21,780
So in performing this technique, we will separate a desired compound from a mixture
所以在进行这项技术时，我们会通过把目标化合物

19
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:24,780
by moving it from one solvent to another.
从一种溶剂转移到另一种溶剂中，把它从混合物中分离出来。

20
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:29,280
To perform this technique, we will be taking the solution and adding a new solvent that
要进行这项技术，我们会取溶液，加入一种新的溶剂，

21
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:33,000
dissolves and isolates one compound from the mixture.
它能溶解并从混合物中分离出一种化合物。

22
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,720
We must use a solvent that is immiscible with the first solvent, so that separate layers
我们必须使用与第一种溶剂互不相溶的溶剂，这样才会

23
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:41,600
will form, as this makes it quite easy to separate them.
形成分开的液层，因为这样分离起来就相当容易。

24
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:44,340
To do this, we'll need a separatory funnel.
为此，我们需要一个分液漏斗。

25
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:49,540
This is a tool that is used to separate two immiscible liquids of different densities.
这是一种用来分离两种密度不同、互不相溶的液体的工具。

26
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:54,760
Once again, in most cases, the two liquids will be an organic solvent, plus whatever compounds
同样，在大多数情况下，这两种液体一种是有机溶剂，加上溶解在其中的

27
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:59,780
are dissolved in it, and then water, plus whatever compounds are dissolved in it.
各种化合物，另一种是水，加上溶解在其中的各种化合物。

28
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:04,340
It is usually the case that the aqueous layer has a greater density than the organic layer,
通常情况下，水层的密度比有机层大，

29
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:08,660
so it goes to the bottom while the organic solvent stays on top, as gravity will pull
所以水层沉在下面，而有机溶剂留在上面，因为重力会以更大的力

30
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:11,580
the denser layer down with greater force.
把密度较大的那层往下拉。

31
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:16,180
However, some organic solvents are more dense than water and will thus occupy the
不过，有些有机溶剂的密度比水大，因此会处于

32
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:21,180
bottom layer, so it is important to consult a table of densities to be sure as to
下层，所以查阅密度表来确认

33
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,060
which layer is which.
哪一层是哪一层很重要。

34
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:27,120
When in doubt, if you want to identify which layer is which, add a bit of water.
拿不准的时候，如果你想确认哪一层是哪一层，就加一点水。

35
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:30,880
Whichever layer grows, that's the aqueous layer.
哪一层变多了，哪一层就是水层。

36
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:34,720
Now let's get more familiar with the intricacies of the separatory funnel.
现在我们来更深入地熟悉分液漏斗的细节。

37
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:40,120
As we can see here, the funnel has a stopper at the top, and a stopcock at the bottom.
我们在这里可以看到，漏斗顶部有一个塞子，底部有一个旋塞。

38
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:43,600
This middle region is where our separation will take place.
中间这个区域就是进行分离的地方。

39
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:47,240
To get this ready, you might have to add a little bit of grease to the stopper and
准备时，你可能需要给塞子和／

40
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:50,280
or stopcock, since they tend to get stuck.
或旋塞涂一点润滑脂，因为它们容易卡住。

41
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:54,620
To set up for the extraction, we'll start with a ring stand attached to a support like
为萃取做准备，我们先把一个铁圈像这样固定在支架

42
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:55,620
this.
上。

43
00:02:55,620 --> 00:03:00,100
We'll then place our separatory funnel in the ring and make sure everything is secure.
然后把分液漏斗放进铁圈里，确保一切都牢固。

44
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:03,620
To verify that the stopcock works, add some water.
为了确认旋塞能正常工作，加一些水。

45
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:07,100
Make sure there are no leaks when the valve is closed.
确保阀门关闭时没有泄漏。

46
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:09,660
Open the valve to see how the water flows.
打开阀门，看看水是怎么流出来的。

47
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:11,860
Once satisfied, remove the water.
确认没问题后，把水倒掉。

48
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:14,340
We are now ready to get started.
现在我们可以开始了。

49
00:03:14,340 --> 00:03:18,600
So let's say this is a reaction mixture that we just got from performing a chemical
假设这是我们刚刚在某种有机溶剂中进行化学

50
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:21,480
reaction in some organic solvent.
反应得到的反应混合物。

51
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:25,840
Most of the time you'll need to quench a reaction once it's finished by adding water.
大多数时候，反应结束后你需要加水来淬灭反应。

52
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:30,900
This means to stop a reaction mixture from reacting further, often with dilute weak acid
意思是让反应混合物不再继续反应，通常用稀的弱酸

53
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:34,480
or base, to neutralize any ionic species.
或弱碱，来中和任何离子物种。

54
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:38,680
This means that after any chemical reaction, you will need to perform an extraction to
这意味着在任何化学反应之后，你都需要进行萃取，

55
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:43,360
separate your organic compounds from whatever is in the aqueous layer.
把你的有机化合物与水层中的东西分开。

56
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:47,960
In this particular case, rather than a reaction mixture, we simply have a mixture containing
在这个具体的例子中，我们用的不是反应混合物，而只是一份含有

57
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:54,680
benzoic acid and 2-methoxy naphthalene dissolved in diethyl ether, and our goal is to obtain
苯甲酸和 2-甲氧基萘、溶解在乙醚中的混合物，我们的目标是得到

58
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:58,560
each of these two compounds in a pure form.
这两种化合物各自的纯净形式。

59
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:02,840
These are both soluble in diethyl ether, but insoluble in water.
它们都溶于乙醚，但不溶于水。

60
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:08,720
However, if we add aqueous base to this mixture, benzoic acid will deprotonate, becoming
不过，如果我们往这个混合物里加入碱的水溶液，苯甲酸就会脱去质子，变成

61
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:14,240
the benzoate anion, which has a formal negative charge, and will thus become water soluble
苯甲酸根阴离子，它带有一个形式负电荷，因此会变得水溶，

62
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:16,880
and move into the aqueous phase.
并转移到水相中。

63
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:21,560
Since 2-methoxy naphthalene will not react, that will remain in the organic phase, and
由于 2-甲氧基萘不会发生反应，它会留在有机相中，这样

64
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:24,700
the two compounds will have separated.
两种化合物就分开了。

65
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:28,560
With our strategy understood, we can begin performing the technique.
理解了策略之后，我们就可以开始操作了。

66
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:33,520
Making sure that the stopcock is closed, let's transfer our mixture to the separatory
确保旋塞是关着的，我们用一个锥形玻璃漏斗把混合物转移到分液

67
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:36,600
funnel using a conical glass funnel.
漏斗中。

68
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:40,460
This is our organic layer.
这是我们的有机层。

69
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:44,340
To make sure we have transferred everything, rinse the beaker that held the mixture with
为了确保把所有东西都转移过去，用乙醚冲洗盛放混合物的烧杯，

70
00:04:44,340 --> 00:04:46,940
ether and transfer that as well.
也一并转移过去。

71
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:51,060
Had this been the product of a chemical reaction, it would already have been quenched and thus
如果这是一个化学反应的产物，它应该已经被淬灭，因而

72
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:53,900
have formed organic and aqueous layers.
已经形成了有机层和水层。

73
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:58,260
But since we are just doing an isolated extraction, let's go ahead and perform the necessary
但由于我们只是做一个单独的萃取，那就直接在分液漏斗里

74
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:01,780
acid base reaction right in the separatory funnel.
进行所需的酸碱反应。

75
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:07,480
To separate benzoic acid from the mixture, we will add 30 milliliters of 1 molar sodium
为了把苯甲酸从混合物中分离出来，我们往分液漏斗中加入 30 毫升 1 摩尔每升的氢氧化钠

76
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:10,240
hydroxide to the separatory funnel.
溶液。

77
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:15,940
This will pass through the organic layer, react with benzoic acid on the way to form
它会穿过有机层，途中与苯甲酸反应生成

78
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:22,580
